feat(landing): rebuild the home page in runkiri.com's design language

The page adopts the official site's art direction: warm paper ground with
deep mustard gold, Bricolage Grotesque headlines, container-wall texture,
stacked hard-shadow cards and a tilted dark app window, in both light and
dark palettes.

Content moves into src/lib/landing.ts and 13 landing components, interaction
is centralised in src/scripts/landing.ts, and every style stays inside the
.kiri scope so docs pages are untouched.

New hands-on benchmark sections: a three-engine startup race (path, slow
motion, play, engine switches, loop, residual processes, reset), a typing and
replayable terminal session, a Share link toggle with its visitor notice, a
memory and sleep model (container count, per-container memory, time scale,
idle threshold, auto demo), and a per-platform architecture switch. All
figures reuse the measured values from this repository's docs.

Animations start and stop with visibility and are torn down on
astro:before-swap so client-side navigation never doubles a timer;
prefers-reduced-motion renders the end state directly.
